      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:1:1:1:3",
      "text": [
        " قُلْتُ لَهُ مَا الْعَقْلُ قَالَ مَا عُبِدَ بِهِ الرَّحْمَنُ وَ اكْتُسِبَ بِهِ الْجِنَانُ قَالَ قُلْتُ فَالَّذِي كَانَ فِي مُعَاوِيَةَ فَقَالَ تِلْكَ النَّكْرَاءُ تِلْكَ الشَّيْطَنَةُ وَ هِيَ شَبِيهَةٌ بِالْعَقْلِ وَ لَيْسَتْ بِالْعَقْلِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ahmad Bin Idrees, from Muhammad Bin Abdul Jabbar, from one of our companions, ",
          "(It has been narrated) raising it to Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, said, ‘I said to him<sup>asws</sup>, ‘What is the ‘الْعَقْلَ’ (<span class=\"iTxt\">Aql</span>- intellect?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Through which the Beneficent is worshipped with, and the Gardens are attained with’. I said, ‘So that which was in Muawiya?’ So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘That is the heinous, that is the devilry, and it may disguise as the intellect, but it is not the intellect’."
        ]
      }
    },
